  - line: 18
    type: narration
    text: "scene 009.5 — epilogue: the deep archives of ironspire"
  - line: 20
    type: narration
    text: "scene meta:"
  - line: 21
    type: narration
    text: "location: Deep places beneath Ironspire"
  - line: 22
    type: narration
    text: "time: three millennia after year 100"
  - line: 23
    type: narration
    text: "participants: Nephoretti scholars (historical framing), future heroes"
  - line: 24
    type: narration
    text: "focus: Epilogue framing explaining how Nephoretti scholars in Ironspire preserved the historical truth of the Sundering, Igigi secret alliance, and setting up the Second Coming (Nephilim summoning) and Fifth Coming future."
  - line: 25
    type: narration
    text: "continuity: Approximately 3,000 years after the morning after departure in scene 009.4; concludes the First Coming arc in chapter 009 and bridges into chapter 010"
  - line: 26
    type: narration
    text: "presentation: cutscene"
  - line: 27
    type: narration
    text: "cutscene purpose: Historical epilogue framing the legacy of the First Coming, the preservation of truth in Ironspire, and future Comings"
  - line: 29
    type: narration
    text: "In the deep places beneath Ironspire, where Nephoretti scholars preserved what the Anunnaki tried to erase, ancient records told a story most had forgotten:"
  - line: 31
    type: narration
    text: "Once, Giants were unified."
  - line: 32
    type: narration
    text: "Once, cooperation between tribes was natural rather than negotiated."
  - line: 33
    type: narration
    text: "Once, before the Sundering, they built wonders that made even Anunnaki infrastructure seem crude."
  - line: 35
    type: narration
    text: "That unity was broken not by conquest but by whispers."
  - line: 36
    type: narration
    text: "By lies so subtle they became truth across generations."
  - line: 37
    type: narration
    text: "By divisions manufactured to serve purposes the victims never recognized until too late."
  - line: 39
    type: narration
    text: "But in those same deep places, other records existed."
  - line: 40
    type: narration
    text: "Igigi chronicles documenting three thousand years of choosing alliance despite programming."
  - line: 41
    type: narration
    text: "Giant oral histories preserving memories of how friendship was built from wreckage."
  - line: 42
    type: narration
    text: "Nephoretti observations of how the Sundering was resisted even when resistance seemed impossible."
  - line: 44
    type: narration
    text: "The Second Coming would test whether that resistance proved sufficient."
  - line: 46
    type: narration
    text: "The Nephilim would be summoned through desperation and barely-sustained cooperation."
  - line: 48
    type: narration
    text: "The alliance would fracture immediately after, some Giants choosing Anunnaki promises over unified resistance."
  - line: 50
    type: narration
    text: "And three thousand years beyond that, in the Fifth Coming that approached like inevitable mathematics, heroes would attempt to heal what the First Coming had broken—to reunite tribes whose division had become cultural identity, to rebuild trust that manufactured lies had shattered, to somehow forge unity from fragmentation that had calcified across geological time."
  - line: 52
    type: narration
    text: "Whether they would succeed remained unwritten."
  - line: 54
    type: narration
    text: "But the fact that they would try—that Igigi and Giants had spent three millennia proving consciousness could resist programming through persistent choice—meant the attempt was possible."
  - line: 56
    type: narration
    text: "And possibility, however slim, was more than the Anunnaki's perfect mathematics had calculated."
  - line: 58
    type: narration
    text: "end of chapter 009-stalemate departure the first coming"

